========================================================================
  PART 3: RECURSIVE STRUCTURE OF G_n
========================================================================

  QUESTION: Does G_n contain G_{n-2} as a subgraph?
  I.e., is there an embedding phi: V(G_{n-2}) -> V(G_n)
  such that adjacent classes in G_{n-2} map to adjacent classes in G_n?

  G_3 has 2 classes: [(0, 1), (1, 3)]

  Fiber of G_3 class 0 (transitive, H=1) in G_5:
    9 classes: [(0, 1), (1, 3), (2, 5), (4, 9), (5, 5), (6, 9), (7, 3), (10, 13), (11, 15)]

  Fiber of G_3 class 1 (3-cycle, H=3) in G_5:
    8 classes: [(2, 5), (3, 3), (4, 9), (5, 5), (6, 9), (8, 11), (9, 15), (11, 15)]

  Edge structure between fibers:
    Cross-fiber edges (f0 -- f1): 32
    Within fiber 0: 18
    Within fiber 1: 14
    Total edges in G_5: 30

