========================================================================
  PART 5: GROWTH TREE n-2 -> n
========================================================================

  The source-sink INSERTION is the reverse of deletion.
  Given inner tournament I (n-2 vertices), add source s and sink t,
  with wiring (source->middle arcs, middle->sink arcs, s-t arc).

  The number of ways to wire = 2^{n-2} * 2^{n-2} * 2 = 2^{2n-3}
  (source-middle: 2^{n-2} choices, middle-sink: 2^{n-2}, s-t direction: 2)

  Growth from n-2=3 to n=5:
  Total wirings per inner class: 2^{2*5-3} = 128

  Inner class 0 (H=1, scores=(0, 1, 2)):
    -> 9 classes at n=5: [(0, 1), (1, 3), (2, 5), (4, 9), (5, 5), (6, 9), (7, 3), (10, 13), (11, 15)]
    Total labeled tournaments above: 824
    Inner labeled: 6, wirings: 128, predicted overcounting: 5*4=20
    Predicted total: 15360 / 20 = 768
    Actual total above: 824

  Inner class 1 (H=3, scores=(1, 1, 1)):
    -> 8 classes at n=5: [(2, 5), (3, 3), (4, 9), (5, 5), (6, 9), (8, 11), (9, 15), (11, 15)]
    Total labeled tournaments above: 704
    Inner labeled: 2, wirings: 128, predicted overcounting: 5*4=20
    Predicted total: 5120 / 20 = 256
    Actual total above: 704


